<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Las Bela State</h1><p class="st-meta">1742 CE – 1955 CE (approx.) · capital Bela</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Baloch coastal principality south of Kalat ruled by the Jams of Las Bela, which joined Pakistan in 1948.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 1742 Jam Ali Khan of the Aliani branch of the Jamot tribe established a ruling house in the Las Bela plain, which lies between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kirthar-mountains">Kirthar range</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabian-sea">Arabian Sea</a>. The state acknowledged the overlordship of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/khanate-of-kalat">Khanate of Kalat</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Jam ruled a small, sparsely populated land of herders and farmers, with the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sonmiani">Sonmiani</a> as its outlet to the sea. Under British paramountcy it was handled through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baluchistan-agency">Baluchistan Agency</a>, and its rulers balanced between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/khanate-of-kalat">Kalat</a> and the British. Its people spoke Lasi, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balochi-language">Balochi</a> and Sindhi.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jam-ghulam-qadir-khan">Jam Ghulam Qadir Khan</a> acceded to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/islamic-republic-of-pakistan">Pakistan</a> in March 1948. Las Bela joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/baluchistan-states-union">Baluchistan States Union</a> in 1952 and was merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-pakistan">West Pakistan</a> in 1955; it is now a district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balochistan">Balochistan</a> province.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/las-bela-state.jpg" alt="Las Bela State" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Mysid · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_State_of_Las_Bela.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1742 CE – 1955 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bela</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Jam Ghulam Qadir Khan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Lasi, Balochi, Sindhi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/pakistan">Pakistan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Las Bela</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1848&amp;focus=las-bela-state" aria-label="Las Bela State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6431 1214 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Las Bela State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6751 1470L6738 1372M6751 1470L7364 1602M6751 1470L6778 1519M6751 1470L6738 1372"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6738 1372h0M7364 1602h0M6778 1519h0M6738 1372h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6751 1470h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6751 1470h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Bela. <a href="/atlas?year=1848&amp;focus=las-bela-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
